# THE P0 DEPLOYMENT LANE IS HASHED BY BYTE, SO ITS BYTES MUST NOT VARY.
#
# `db/manifest.toml` pins a SHA-256 over each deployment file's contents, and
# `deploy-fresh.mjs` refuses to run when a hash does not match. Those pins are
# the LF bytes stored in git.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`, which
# rewrites LF to CRLF at checkout. That changes every byte-count and every
# hash: `db/schema/0001_p0_baseline.sql` pins 0c095c46… (the git blob) and
# hashed db440b4d… on a Windows working tree, so `npm run db:verify:p0` failed
# on Windows while passing in the Codespace.
#
# The consequence is worse than a failing check. If the manifest were ever
# regenerated from a Windows tree the pins would become CRLF hashes, the
# Codespace replay would then fail instead, and which platform is authoritative
# would depend on who last touched it. Pinning the line endings makes the
# deployment lane byte-identical everywhere and the hashes platform-invariant.
#
# Scoped deliberately to the P0 lane rather than applied repo-wide: other
# branches are in flight, and renormalising every file would collide with them.

db/**/*.sql       text eol=lf
db/manifest.toml  text eol=lf

# The runners that read and hash those files, kept in the same regime.
scripts/p0-target.mjs                     text eol=lf
scripts/p0-run.mjs                        text eol=lf
scripts/deploy-fresh.mjs                  text eol=lf
scripts/verify-p0.mjs                     text eol=lf
scripts/verify-deployment-determinism.mjs text eol=lf

# Evidence is compared and quoted; keep it stable too.
docs/evidence/p0/*.json text eol=lf
docs/evidence/p0/*.md   text eol=lf
